A preliminary enquiry is a fact-finding enquiry [(DP (P&A) Rule 15(1), PDF p. 22)](https://indiacode.gov.in/server/api/core/bitstreams/2188ca35-06ec-46d7-84ef-210bfa017c71/content#page=22). Its purpose is to:

- establish the nature of the default and identify the defaulter or defaulters;
- collect prosecution evidence;
- judge the quantum of default;
- bring relevant documents on record to help a regular departmental enquiry.

Where specific information on these points already exists, no preliminary enquiry is needed and the disciplinary authority may order a departmental enquiry straight away. In all other cases a preliminary enquiry should normally come first [(DP (P&A) Rule 15(1), PDF p. 22)](https://indiacode.gov.in/server/api/core/bitstreams/2188ca35-06ec-46d7-84ef-210bfa017c71/content#page=22).
